# Development

## Purpose

The Development documentation supports the implementation of Financial Friday.

Unlike the Foundation and Advisor documentation, which define the product and its architecture, the Development documents capture the day-to-day engineering process.

Topics include:

- Sprint planning
- Meeting notes
- Architectural decisions
- Product decisions
- Coding standards
- Release history

---

# Sections

## Architecture

Working architectural notes and Architecture Decision Records (ADRs).

## Meetings

Meeting notes and design discussions.

## Planning

Sprint planning, feature backlog, and implementation planning.

## Product

Product-related decisions, copy, branding, and design philosophy.

## Release Notes

Project changelog and release history.

---

# Guiding Principle

Development documentation should explain _why_ engineering decisions were made, not simply record _what_ changed.
